WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.133 --> 00:00:01.368
Big developments this morning

00:00:01.368 --> 00:00:02.769
and two different investigations

00:00:02.769 --> 00:00:03.937
into former President Trump,

00:00:03.937 --> 00:00:04.471
the election

00:00:04.471 --> 00:00:06.239
interference probe in Georgia

00:00:06.239 --> 00:00:07.240
and the Stormy Daniels

00:00:07.240 --> 00:00:08.475
hush money investigation.

00:00:08.475 --> 00:00:09.376
Here in New York,

00:00:09.376 --> 00:00:10.443
we are now learning

00:00:10.443 --> 00:00:11.878
there's another recording

00:00:11.878 --> 00:00:13.046
of former President Trump

00:00:13.046 --> 00:00:15.181
pressuring another Georgia official

00:00:15.181 --> 00:00:16.016
to help overturn

00:00:16.016 --> 00:00:17.617
his election loss this time.

00:00:17.617 --> 00:00:18.118
It's a phone

00:00:18.118 --> 00:00:18.752
call with the state's

00:00:18.752 --> 00:00:19.953
Republican House speaker

00:00:19.953 --> 00:00:21.187
and here in New York City.

00:00:21.187 --> 00:00:22.088
Stormy Daniels met

00:00:22.088 --> 00:00:23.223
with prosecutors yesterday

00:00:23.223 --> 00:00:23.623
as they near

00:00:23.623 --> 00:00:25.759
the end of that investigation.

00:00:25.759 --> 00:00:26.693
Trump's former fixer,

00:00:26.693 --> 00:00:27.327
Michael Cohen,

00:00:27.327 --> 00:00:29.162
also finished testifying yesterday

00:00:29.162 --> 00:00:30.530
before the Grand jury.

00:00:30.530 --> 00:00:31.831
That makes two appearances

00:00:31.831 --> 00:00:33.033
from him in a week.

00:00:33.033 --> 00:00:33.967
Cohen will join us

00:00:33.967 --> 00:00:35.535
right here on CNN this morning

00:00:35.535 --> 00:00:37.270
in the 8:00 hour.

00:00:37.270 --> 00:00:39.372
Let's get caught up on all of this.

00:00:39.372 --> 00:00:40.540
With our senior legal affairs

00:00:40.540 --> 00:00:41.541
correspondent, Paula Reid.

00:00:41.541 --> 00:00:41.975
Wow.

00:00:41.975 --> 00:00:44.544
So much in just a few days, right?

00:00:44.577 --> 00:00:47.080
Even by Donald Trump's standards.

00:00:47.280 --> 00:00:50.316
Yesterday was a wild day in court for him

00:00:50.316 --> 00:00:51.151
and related to a court

00:00:51.151 --> 00:00:52.619
proceedings in Georgia.

00:00:52.619 --> 00:00:53.787
We had these members

00:00:53.787 --> 00:00:54.854
of the special grand jury

00:00:54.854 --> 00:00:56.289
revealing these incredible details

00:00:56.289 --> 00:00:57.390
of the investigation.

00:00:57.390 --> 00:00:58.458
And then here in New York,

00:00:58.458 --> 00:01:00.060
you had his former alleged mistress

00:01:00.060 --> 00:01:02.962
and his fixer both talking to prosecutors

00:01:05.165 --> 00:01:06.466
two investigations

00:01:06.466 --> 00:01:08.234
into former President Donald Trump

00:01:08.234 --> 00:01:09.069
heating up

00:01:09.069 --> 00:01:10.670
with possible indictments

00:01:10.670 --> 00:01:12.605
coming down soon.

00:01:12.605 --> 00:01:13.540
In New York,

00:01:13.540 --> 00:01:14.207
the Manhattan

00:01:14.207 --> 00:01:15.542
district attorney's office

00:01:15.542 --> 00:01:16.743
speaking on Wednesday

00:01:16.743 --> 00:01:18.711
to two key witnesses

00:01:18.711 --> 00:01:20.246
as part of its investigation

00:01:20.246 --> 00:01:20.980
into hush money

00:01:20.980 --> 00:01:21.781
payments

00:01:21.781 --> 00:01:24.250
made to adult film star Stormy Daniels

00:01:24.918 --> 00:01:27.087
My position is that

00:01:27.087 --> 00:01:27.921
at the end of the day,

00:01:27.921 --> 00:01:30.690
Donald Trump needs to be held accountable

00:01:30.757 --> 00:01:32.092
for his dirty deeds.

00:01:32.092 --> 00:01:32.725
If, in fact,

00:01:32.725 --> 00:01:34.961
that's the way that the facts play out.

00:01:35.395 --> 00:01:36.763
Trump's former fixer

00:01:36.763 --> 00:01:38.932
and personal attorney, Michael Cohen,

00:01:38.932 --> 00:01:40.700
concluded a second day

00:01:40.700 --> 00:01:42.702
of testimony Wednesday,

00:01:42.702 --> 00:01:44.704
and Daniels attorney tweeted

00:01:44.704 --> 00:01:46.206
that she also answered

00:01:46.206 --> 00:01:47.740
prosecutors questions

00:01:47.740 --> 00:01:48.508
and has agreed

00:01:48.508 --> 00:01:51.044
to make herself available as a witness.

00:01:51.411 --> 00:01:52.412
The investigation

00:01:52.412 --> 00:01:53.813
is at a critical juncture

00:01:53.813 --> 00:01:55.615
after the district attorney's office

00:01:55.615 --> 00:01:58.118
invited Trump to testify last week.

00:01:58.618 --> 00:01:58.985
Trump's

00:01:58.985 --> 00:02:01.621
legal team says he will not testify,

00:02:01.788 --> 00:02:03.690
and they're proclaiming his innocence

00:02:03.690 --> 00:02:04.691
with one of his lawyers

00:02:04.691 --> 00:02:06.926
making this striking prediction.

00:02:06.926 --> 00:02:08.928
If his client is indicted,

00:02:08.928 --> 00:02:10.830
I think it will will ultimately embolden

00:02:10.830 --> 00:02:12.065
him, embolden his supporters

00:02:12.065 --> 00:02:13.800
and give him more strength

00:02:13.800 --> 00:02:14.901
because it will be proven

00:02:14.901 --> 00:02:16.336
to be wrongly accused.

00:02:16.336 --> 00:02:17.704
But on the other hand,

00:02:17.704 --> 00:02:18.438
who in their right mind

00:02:18.438 --> 00:02:19.606
wants to be indicted in charge?

00:02:19.606 --> 00:02:20.340
False from the crime?

00:02:20.340 --> 00:02:21.241
Nobody.

00:02:21.241 --> 00:02:23.109
Over in Fulton County, Georgia,

00:02:23.109 --> 00:02:24.844
the Atlanta Journal-Constitution

00:02:24.844 --> 00:02:26.279
is reporting the grand jury

00:02:26.279 --> 00:02:28.982
there heard a recording of a conversation

00:02:28.982 --> 00:02:29.949
between Trump

00:02:29.949 --> 00:02:32.252
and the late former Georgia House Speaker

00:02:32.418 --> 00:02:34.654
David Ralston. In the recording.

00:02:34.821 --> 00:02:35.922
Trump is pushing

00:02:35.922 --> 00:02:36.556
for the speaker

00:02:36.556 --> 00:02:38.224
to call a special session

00:02:38.224 --> 00:02:40.727
to overturn Joe Biden's win in the state.

00:02:41.427 --> 00:02:43.663
One of the jurors recalled Ralston

00:02:43.830 --> 00:02:45.999
basically caught the president off,

00:02:45.999 --> 00:02:46.799
telling Trump,

00:02:46.799 --> 00:02:48.668
I will do everything in my power

00:02:48.668 --> 00:02:50.770
that I think is appropriate.

00:02:50.770 --> 00:02:52.572
The Atlanta Journal-Constitution

00:02:52.572 --> 00:02:54.307
spoke with five jurors

00:02:54.307 --> 00:02:55.742
who served on a grand jury

00:02:55.742 --> 00:02:56.776
investigating Trump's

00:02:56.776 --> 00:02:57.911
actions in Georgia

00:02:57.911 --> 00:03:00.146
after the 2020 election.

00:03:00.146 --> 00:03:02.015
One of those jurors says

00:03:02.015 --> 00:03:02.815
they were presented

00:03:02.815 --> 00:03:04.450
testimony about a meeting

00:03:04.450 --> 00:03:05.685
then Senator and Trump

00:03:05.685 --> 00:03:07.320
ally David Perdue

00:03:07.320 --> 00:03:08.821
had with Republican Governor

00:03:08.821 --> 00:03:10.223
Brian Kemp in December.

00:03:10.223 --> 00:03:13.593
2020 or Camp was also urged to convene

00:03:13.593 --> 00:03:14.894
a special session

00:03:14.894 --> 00:03:16.930
to challenge Biden's election win.

00:03:17.397 --> 00:03:19.265
You know what I'm saying or

00:03:19.265 --> 00:03:20.833
really extraordinary insight

00:03:20.833 --> 00:03:22.569
into the grand jury process there.

00:03:22.569 --> 00:03:24.304
This is not the kind of information

00:03:24.304 --> 00:03:25.638
we usually get, particularly before

00:03:25.638 --> 00:03:27.440
there's been any sort of indictment

00:03:27.440 --> 00:03:28.875
that we know this grand jury

00:03:28.875 --> 00:03:30.510
has recommended multiple indictments.

00:03:30.510 --> 00:03:31.878
And if you talk to the former president's

00:03:31.878 --> 00:03:32.712
legal team,

00:03:32.712 --> 00:03:34.714
they are concerned about Georgia

00:03:34.714 --> 00:03:36.182
in terms of charges being brought.

00:03:36.182 --> 00:03:36.816
They are not.

00:03:36.816 --> 00:03:37.717
However, they say

00:03:37.717 --> 00:03:39.452
worried about a conviction.

00:03:39.452 --> 00:03:40.787
Paula. Fascinating.

00:03:40.787 --> 00:03:42.355
Wild as you said, even.

00:03:42.355 --> 00:03:43.223
I don't know how you compare

00:03:43.223 --> 00:03:44.991
Trump standard with all of these.

00:03:44.991 --> 00:03:45.758
It's a lot of coffee

00:03:45.758 --> 00:03:47.927
rain in Brainiac over here.

00:03:47.961 --> 00:03:49.195
Thank you, Paula.

00:03:49.195 --> 00:03:50.263
This is why The New Yorker

00:03:50.263 --> 00:03:51.664
is one of several investigates

00:03:51.664 --> 00:03:52.232
of Donald Trump

00:03:52.232 --> 00:03:53.399
new development and another one,

00:03:53.399 --> 00:03:54.400
which is the Fulton County

00:03:54.400 --> 00:03:56.035
special grand jury.

00:03:56.035 --> 00:03:56.803
We now know

00:03:56.803 --> 00:03:58.171
from Atlanta Journal-Constitution

00:03:58.171 --> 00:03:59.505
reporting that there was a third

00:03:59.505 --> 00:04:00.106
Trump call.

00:04:00.106 --> 00:04:01.441
We knew of two previous Trump calls

00:04:01.441 --> 00:04:02.308
the most infamous one

00:04:02.308 --> 00:04:03.209
is to Brad Raffensperger,

00:04:03.209 --> 00:04:04.244
the secretary of state.

00:04:04.244 --> 00:04:04.911
There was another one

00:04:04.911 --> 00:04:06.112
to one of the investigators.

00:04:06.112 --> 00:04:07.880
And now we know there was a phone call

00:04:07.880 --> 00:04:08.982
to the late speaker

00:04:08.982 --> 00:04:10.283
of the Georgia House of Representatives

00:04:10.283 --> 00:04:11.117
trying to get the speaker

00:04:11.117 --> 00:04:12.018
to bring the legislature

00:04:12.018 --> 00:04:13.519
back in to help Donald Trump.

00:04:13.519 --> 00:04:14.254
What does that mean

00:04:14.254 --> 00:04:15.588
if you're building a case?

00:04:15.588 --> 00:04:15.822
I guess

00:04:15.822 --> 00:04:16.956
if you're Trump, you could make the case

00:04:16.956 --> 00:04:18.224
if you had one phone call.

00:04:18.224 --> 00:04:18.758
He was upset.

00:04:18.758 --> 00:04:20.226
He lost the election. He was venting.

00:04:20.226 --> 00:04:21.427
He didn't mean anything. Nefarious.

00:04:21.427 --> 00:04:22.795
If you have three phone calls

00:04:22.795 --> 00:04:23.730
where he's asking for help

00:04:23.730 --> 00:04:24.764
overturning the results.

00:04:24.764 --> 00:04:26.232
How powerful is that evidence?

00:04:26.232 --> 00:04:28.301
Well, so what the prosecutors, if again,

00:04:28.334 --> 00:04:28.835
this is

00:04:28.835 --> 00:04:30.903
in the pre indictment stage,

00:04:30.903 --> 00:04:32.905
in this investigation in Georgia as well,

00:04:32.905 --> 00:04:34.474
if they decided to bring the case,

00:04:34.474 --> 00:04:35.041
then that would be

00:04:35.041 --> 00:04:36.376
another piece of evidence

00:04:36.376 --> 00:04:37.443
that they could use

00:04:37.443 --> 00:04:39.512
to indicate that he had the intent

00:04:39.679 --> 00:04:40.113
to try

00:04:40.113 --> 00:04:42.415
to violate Georgia's election laws,

00:04:42.415 --> 00:04:43.916
which is what this Georgia case

00:04:43.916 --> 00:04:45.118
is all about.

00:04:45.118 --> 00:04:46.552
And so, again,

00:04:46.552 --> 00:04:48.488
another near decision point.

00:04:48.488 --> 00:04:50.356
We believe when we get to decisions,

00:04:50.356 --> 00:04:51.424
we'll have more interesting covers,

00:04:51.424 --> 00:04:52.825
even more interesting conversations.

